00:14:30.991 --> 00:14:33.201
I'm really curious to find
out what you have to say.

00:14:33.201 --> 00:14:34.451
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:14:34.451 --> 00:14:36.602
to the LonelyBookaneer, thank you so much

00:14:36.602 --> 00:14:38.861
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word,

00:14:38.861 --> 00:14:41.205
and posting the review
on your YouTube channel.

00:14:41.205 --> 00:14:42.658
I really, really appreciate the support

00:14:42.658 --> 00:14:45.445
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed my book.

00:14:45.445 --> 00:14:47.374
- [Man] In this video I'll
be talking about the book,

00:14:47.374 --> 00:14:50.017
Your One Word by Evan Carmichael.

00:14:50.017 --> 00:14:51.662
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:51.662 --> 00:14:54.020
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:57.061
in yourself, and whatever
your one word is,

00:14:57.061 --> 00:14:59.478
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:15:05.843 --> 00:15:08.134
- Me and a buddy growing up in school,

00:15:08.134 --> 00:15:10.445
John Zanner was his name, we would,

00:15:10.445 --> 00:15:12.922
we would try and top each other.

00:15:12.922 --> 00:15:14.649
Every day like, "Hey,
look what I learned."

00:15:14.649 --> 00:15:16.264
And "Oh, well look what I got."

00:15:16.264 --> 00:15:18.993
And "Oh, damn," then I'd go
back and learn something else

00:15:18.993 --> 00:15:21.352
and then he'd go, "Eh!", so the great

00:15:21.352 --> 00:15:24.604
high school competition
got us to another level,

00:15:24.604 --> 00:15:27.324
which was great, and then
at some point it was like,

00:15:27.324 --> 00:15:29.991
"Wow, the guys I'm playing with,

00:15:31.029 --> 00:15:33.539
"I need to play with better players."

00:15:33.539 --> 00:15:35.896
And I was writing, I wrote some songs.

00:15:35.896 --> 00:15:38.588
They didn't like them, they
just wanted to play covers.

00:15:38.588 --> 00:15:40.407
And then I kind of decided,
"Well, I got to start

00:15:40.407 --> 00:15:42.177
"playing with other people."

00:15:42.177 --> 00:15:44.988
So right then I kind of
knew that I was on a quest

00:15:44.988 --> 00:15:46.589
and I wanted to get better.

00:15:46.589 --> 00:15:48.464
And some friends didn't understand that.

00:15:48.464 --> 00:15:51.821
They just, "Why don't you
just hang out with us?"

00:15:51.821 --> 00:15:54.654
And I was on a quest to go places.

00:15:55.771 --> 00:15:57.799
I think it was my sophomore year,

00:15:57.799 --> 00:16:01.571
I went back to high
school, the summertime,

00:16:01.571 --> 00:16:03.936
to gear up to start
playing football again.

00:16:03.936 --> 00:16:05.822
And I had long hair at that point,

00:16:05.822 --> 00:16:08.747
and the coach said, "You
have to get a haircut."

00:16:08.747 --> 00:16:12.537
And I said, "Yeah, but Eddie
Van Halen's got long hair

00:16:12.537 --> 00:16:14.691
"and Michael Schenker's got long hair.

00:16:14.691 --> 00:16:16.744
"I want to play football
and have long hair."

00:16:16.744 --> 00:16:19.029
"You can't do it," so
right then it was one

00:16:19.029 --> 00:16:22.789
of those forks in the road
that was pretty pivotal

00:16:22.789 --> 00:16:26.257
in my life that I had no clue about.

00:16:26.257 --> 00:16:29.256
And I kind of just
said, "Well, screw this.

00:16:29.256 --> 00:16:32.293
"Do I want to be second
string playing football

00:16:32.293 --> 00:16:36.210
"or do I want to be up
on stage with a mission,

00:16:37.453 --> 00:16:39.536
"speaking through music?"

00:16:40.668 --> 00:16:41.777
I didn't know it at the time

00:16:41.777 --> 00:16:43.748
but it was pretty much the right choice.

